WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.900
Who would be their main football rival?

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:04.820
I believe it was Ole Miss and Alabama.

3
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.780
You know Ole Miss and Alabama?

4
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.980
Was that due to the team, the school, or the coach?

5
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:18.920
The . . . Well, Ole Miss was just, you know, they . . . All you heard from the fifties on,

6
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.240
going to the games, was chants from the LSU fans, “Go to hell, Ole Miss!”

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.505
It’s one of the first times I ever heard “hell” in my life [laughs].

8
00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:30.680
Here are all these people just really saying it out loud and screaming it in public.

9
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.080
But they did.

10
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.560
They were just really had it in for Ole Miss.

11
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.480
Why, I don’t know.

12
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.180
They just did.

13
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.300
There was just an energy charge between the two.

14
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.100
They just . . . They just had it in for each other.

15
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.580
And Alabama . . . Bear Bryant was such an esteemed coach.

16
00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.980
He was wonderful to watch.

17
00:00:48.980 --> 00:01:00.620
You enjoyed watching him coach a game and . . . The thing about Alabama that really kind of got everybody’s goat was every time their team would make a touchdown,

18
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.400
their cheerleaders would get at the end.

19
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.860
And I mean, they would get on their knees and they would praise them.

20
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.120
I don’t know if they still do this today, but all the cheerleaders would be on their knees lined up at the end,

21
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.060
right by where they had scored and they would have their hands up in the air.

22
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.380
Then they would all go down and their face would touch the ground.

23
00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.440
Then they would come up with their hands up in the air.

24
00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.340
And they were praising their team.

25
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.880
Oh, that used to just make LSU so mad!

26
00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.560
I think that’s why they were a rival.

27
00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.840
Of course, they were good, too.

28
00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.960
They beat us a lot, you know.
